WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Everything we invested
our energy into

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.480
and our hearts into,

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.600
it turned into something
that changed the world.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.320
I can't say

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.720
that I immediately
jumped into the process

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.680
with an outline in mind.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.240
How will I write
so that people believe me?

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.920
And how will I write it
so that they understand me?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.320
I think that's
a natural thing to feel

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.040
when you sit down
to write any book,

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.280
but especially a memoir.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.800
I wanted to feel
recognized as a person.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.600
But I also wanted to be
understood as a writer.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.440
I wanted people
to understand

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.240
why the people around me
believed what they believed

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.040
and why they behaved
the way they behaved,

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:40.480
and why I couldn't
even hold it against them.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.400
What you learn in the
first third of Unorthodox

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.600
is an internal

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.200
process of questioning
and doubting

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.600
that occurs in the mind
of the protagonist.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:54.040
At the end of the day,
the story was

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.720
about a woman's body.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.920
And so when I first
started writing,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.120
that was
the part I wrote about,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.520
and it was originally
from my blog.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:03.680
It was… That was, for me,
the center of my story.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.640
I went back into the past
and I plucked

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.840
episodes from my life

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.600
and I

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.480
sorted them

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.960
chronologically,
next to each other

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.000
in order to build
some kind of arc.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.600
I remember talking
to a Japanese reporter

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.400
when the Japanese edition
of Unorthodox

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.840
was released as a book,

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.440
and she was telling me,

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.880
"Do you know that the story

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.840
of every Japanese woman's
life is Unorthodox?"

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.920
She started to cry.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.200
It's almost like,

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.560
instead of this just being

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.640
my weird,
unusual life experience,

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.240
it's now part
of a universal spectrum

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.760
of the experiences of women.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.280
Wherever I go and talk
to people in the industry,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.600
they're, like,
"You should never think

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.240
of your readers
when you're writing.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.520
You shouldn't write
for your readers,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.840
you should always write
for you."

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.000
And I broke that rule.
I broke so many rules.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.160
I broke so many rules.

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.800
My book should never
have been successful

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.080
considering
how many rules I broke,

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.720
but I thought about
my readers all the time.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.640
They were the ones
I wanted to reach.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.480
There is no reason
for a woman

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:09.760
to experience shame
as a result

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.360
of this very common,
lived body experience.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:17.640
And that, to me,
is what I think

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.840
touched a nerve for women
all over the world.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.240
I feel

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.360
as if I have been
emancipated

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.960
from my own story.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.600
I think that's
the power of storytelling.

